{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Frozen before the seed exists: raw register value -> group and answer. A raw value that is not in a country's status table is skipped (status_not_mapped), never judged by hand. Keys are compared in lower case with spaces collapsed. The owner completes the tables from data/benchmark2/frames.json (probe) before the freeze; tools/bench2_prereg.py freeze refuses while a probed status is missing here.",
  "skip_reasons": {
    "legal_form": "legal form not allowed",
    "status_not_mapped": "raw status (or insolvency case type) not in the mapping table",
    "ambiguous": "ambiguous register facts: a strike-off proposal, a past insolvency case on an active company, a procedure the status field does not settle, or listing and record that disagree",
    "sanctions_name": "its name appears on a sanctions list (a number match puts it in group S instead)",
    "pilot": "used in the pilot"
  },
  "entry_format": "status entries: {group, status, insolvent} or {skip: reason}. insolvent is true, false, null (the register does not say: not scored) or \"from_cases\": true when any case type maps to true, else null when one maps to null, else false; with no case at all the entry's no_cases value applies (\"skip\" = ambiguous). requires_no_cases: any case makes the company ambiguous.",
